---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = "Fallen Lineage Trello Board – What Each List Means";
const description = "Access the official Fallen Lineage Trello link and board directory. Learn what each column covers, from roadmap plans and cards to official Discord links.";
const h1 = "Fallen Lineage Trello";

const siblingLinks = [
  { title: "Roblox Codes", href: "/codes", desc: "Redeem active promo codes for free rolls." },
  { title: "Class Tier List", href: "/tier-list", desc: "Check community rankings and meta picks." },
  { title: "Classes Guide", href: "/classes", desc: "Learn individual skills and scaling mechanics." }
];

const lastUpdatedDate = "November 16, 2026";
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  h1={h1}
  siblingLinks={siblingLinks}
>
  <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    <span class="badge badge-amber">Official Reference</span>
    <h1 style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">{h1}</h1>
    <div class="meta-banner">
      <span><strong>Source:</strong> Official Development Hub</span>
      <span>&bull;</span>
      <span><strong>Verified:</strong> {lastUpdatedDate}</span>
    </div>
    <p>
      The official <strong>Fallen Lineage Trello</strong> board is the primary developer-maintained information hub. Learn how to locate the official link, interpret development cards, and read upcoming patch roadmaps accurately.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Official Trello Board Access</h2>
    <p>
      Fallen Lineage developers host their public cards directly on Trello to maintain transparency with the Roblox community.
    </p>
    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-primary);">Accessing the Official Link Safely</h3>
      <p>
        Always obtain the Trello link directly from the verified Roblox game page or the developer's official Discord server. Avoid searching generic forums to protect your account from phishing replicas.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
        <strong>Board Status:</strong> Public Read-Only (No login required to view cards or attachments).
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>What Each Column (List) Means</h2>
    <p>
      The Fallen Lineage board is organized into specific lists arranged from general information to complex mechanics:
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-2" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
      <div class="card">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent-amber-light);">1. Information & Rules</h3>
        <p>Contains general guidelines, developer credits, official group links, and core terminology explaining turn-based combat mechanics.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent-amber-light);">2. Roadmap & Upcoming Patches</h3>
        <p>Highlights features currently in active development, including upcoming class masteries, new dungeon biomes, and UI overhauls.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent-amber-light);">3. Classes & Abilities</h3>
        <p>The definitive list of class cards detailing base damage multipliers, mana costs, skill tree requirements, and unlock shrines.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent-amber-light);">4. Items, Weapons & Relics</h3>
        <p>Comprehensive stat cards for dropped loot, rarity tiers, consumable potion effects, and dungeon drop rates.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent-amber-light);">5. Bosses & Enemies</h3>
        <p>Tactical breakdown of dungeon encounters, boss phase triggers, special attack patterns, and resistance profiles.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--accent-amber-light);">6. Bug Tracker & Known Issues</h3>
        <p>Active issues acknowledged by the dev team with tags indicating whether a fix is scheduled for the next patch cycle.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>How to Track Game Updates Using Trello</h2>
    <p>
      To anticipate meta shifts and build changes before they go live in-game:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Check Card Badges:</strong> Look for updated timestamp labels or colored labels (e.g., green for completed, orange for testing).</li>
      <li><strong>Inspect Card Descriptions:</strong> Developers often update raw formulas inside card descriptions days before deploying the server patch.</li>
      <li><strong>Cross-Check with Our Tier List:</strong> Use previewed balance tweaks to plan your next character reroll using our <a href="/tier-list">Class Tier List</a>.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 3rem;">
    <h2>Official Discord Community Access</h2>
    <p>
      While Trello serves as the reference encyclopedia, the <strong>Official Discord</strong> is where live interaction happens:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Live Code Releases:</strong> New promotional rewards are announced first in `#announcements`—be sure to grab them on our <a href="/codes">Roblox Codes</a> page.</li>
      <li><strong>Developer Q&A:</strong> Weekly balance discussions and community suggestion forums.</li>
      <li><strong>Guild & Co-op Finder:</strong> Form parties with experienced players to conquer hardcore multiplayer dungeons.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
